# {{.Project}} — generated LiveKit Agents project

Generated by `unmute compile` (LiveKit driver). Model routes, prompts, agents,
tasks, and tools come from the source package. Entry agent: `{{.EntryClass}}`.

## Run

Install the generated dependencies, copy the environment template, and start
the LiveKit development worker.

```sh
uv sync                       # or: pip install -e .
cp .env.example .env.local    # then fill in the selected provider values
uv run agent.py console       # local terminal session
uv run agent.py dev           # LiveKit development worker
```

## Trace with Langfuse

Tracing is optional. Set `LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY`, `LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY`, and
`LANGFUSE_BASE_URL` together in `.env.local` to export LiveKit spans. Leaving
all three empty disables tracing. The trace name is
`{{.EntryClass}}-{{.Project}}`; the LiveKit room name becomes the Langfuse
session ID.

Starting the worker or exporting a synthetic span proves connectivity only.
Complete at least one user turn before reviewing the trace. A traced request
contains `llm_node` and `llm_request` generation observations in addition to
the session and agent spans.

Do not edit this project by hand — it is regenerated from the agent spec.
Change the spec and recompile.
